# known gap (todo/t0941) — SELF-HOST lane UNDER-rejects D53 on an IMPORTED
# struct's unique-lock field.
#
# `h.lock` is a field sub-place of `Mutex[int]`. D53 gives it no clone path and
# D10(a) forbids a bare `^` on a sub-place, so the only meaning-preserving
# verdict is E_MoveWithoutOperator — which the Rust lane emits.
#
# The self-host ACCEPTS it and emits C. Both of its expression resolvers
# (`infer_expr_type` and the structural `lvalue_value_type`) type a field place
# through `types.variant_field_types`, keyed `"{StructName}.{field}"`, and that
# table has no row for a struct defined in another module — so the lookup misses,
# the type comes back NO_TYPE, and `is_unique_lock_type` answers false. The SAME
# shape with the struct declared LOCALLY rejects correctly
# (`d53_unique_lock/mutex_field_local_push_reject.gg`), and so does the GENERIC
# local form (`d53_unique_lock/mutex_generic_struct_field_push_reject.gg`) — so
# the axis that discriminates is CROSS-MODULE, not generic-vs-concrete.
#
# The fix is upstream of both resolvers: populate `variant_field_types` for
# imported struct defs (or give the safety walk a complete per-struct field
# registry, as the Rust lane has in `struct_field_names` + `DefInfo.field_types`).
# Do NOT patch it at either read site — that would be two copies of the same
# repair, and this is exactly the "one source of truth per axis" boundary.
#
# INTENDED behaviour (what the `#[ignore]`d test asserts): rejected, with
# E_MoveWithoutOperator naming `Shared[Mutex[T]]`.
from std.collections import Vector
from holder import XHolder

void main():
    XHolder h = XHolder(Mutex[int](5), 1)
    Vector[Mutex[int]] v = Vector[Mutex[int]]()
    v.push(h.lock)
    print(v.len())
